The main Linux behavior appears covered, but the new snapshot self-check uses GNU-only `readlink -f`, which makes the pre-commit guard ineffective on macOS/BSD environments the repo otherwise accommodates.

Review comment:

- [P2] Avoid GNU-only readlink in the snapshot guard — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh3-remainder/scripts/check-design-refs.sh:320-320
  When this pre-commit path runs on macOS/BSD, `/usr/bin/readlink` does not support `-f`; both substitutions here fail to empty strings, so the comparison passes and the guard no longer proves that `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` resolved inside `$SNAPSHOT` (while also printing readlink errors into hook output). This repo already avoids `readlink -f` in other scripts for macOS portability, so use a portable `cd && pwd -P`/helper normalization here instead of disabling the self-check on those environments.
